    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "Carla Bruni, born Carla Gilberta Bruni Tedeschi on 23 December 1967, is an Italian and French singer, songwriter and fashion model who served as first lady of France from 2008 to 2012.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385089107:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:18Z",
      "text": "Carla Bruni was born on 23 December 1967 in Turin.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q143945:P569",
        "wd:Q143945:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:26Z",
      "text": "She was educated at Lycée Janson-de-Sailly, University of Paris 1 Pantheon-Sorbonne and École Jeannine Manuel.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q143945:P69:Q1431541",
        "wd:Q143945:P69:Q999763",
        "wd:Q143945:P69:Q3577715"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:30Z",
      "text": "Records show she has worked in Paris.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q143945:P937:Q90"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:36Z",
      "text": "Wikidata lists 6 awards, among them Grand Cross of the National Order of Benin (2010) and Officer of Arts and Letters (2020).",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q143945:P166:Q94440635",
        "wd:Q143945:P166:Q13452524"
      ]
    },
    {
